# --- Orchestrator monitoring ---------------------------------------------
# The shared monitoring module is stateless, and as of 2026-07-28 it is
# ENFORCED rather than tolerated: status.sh exits 2 instead of spooling into
# the module dir, and both daemons exit 1 rather than falling back to it. The
# two ignore lines that used to sanction that leak
# (.claude/shared/monitoring/{events.jsonl,.watcher-state.json}) are gone on
# purpose — tests/test_bootstrap.py asserts they stay gone, so the behaviour
# cannot quietly return under cover of an ignore rule.

# LEGACY DEFENCE (kept deliberately, G9/LAYOUT-4). Per-task orchestration run
# state is local working data, kept on disk for monitor replay and the Mongo
# legacy keyspace but no longer versioned (untracked 2026-07-27). Since the
# tasks-root move the live tree is `.touch/local-orchestrators/`, ignored by the
# `/.touch/*` rule below; these three lines stay so a RE-CREATED old tree is
# still ignored rather than silently offered for commit. They also remain in the
# verbatim guard lists in tests/test_bootstrap.py and monitoring's test_shell.py.
.claude/local-orchestrators/
.claude/local-orchestrators/*/*.log
.claude/local-orchestrators/*/.watcher-state.json

# --- Touch runtime state --------------------------------------------------
# `.touch/` holds several trust classes in one directory, so the rule is an
# ALLOWLIST: everything under it is ignored, and exactly one file is
# re-included by name.
#
# PROVENANCE (2026-07-31): there used to be a SECOND carve here — three lines
# re-including `.touch/memory/*.md`, Claude Code's auto memory, as a tracked
# subtree (G9/GD-16). It was WITHDRAWN. The memory home still lives at
# `.touch/memory` and nothing about the CLI feature changed; the files are
# simply local state now rather than a published subtree, and the eight that
# had been committed were purged from history in the same change-set. Do not
# "restore" those lines: the twin entry lists in tests/test_bootstrap.py and
# tests/monitoring/test_shell.py were updated alongside this file and now
# assert their ABSENCE, so a well-meaning revert fails three suites.
/.touch/*
/.touch?*/
# The ONE carve (D-12/SKILLS-7): the tracked per-project run constants —
# targeted/full test commands, the known baseline, the review checklist — that
# `touch-run start` merges UNDER a run spec before handing `args` to a workflow
# template. It is configuration, not state, and it is a single FILE, so no
# directory re-include is needed. Never widen this carve: a token file or a
# watcher checkpoint must never become committable.
!/.touch/run.json
*.pid

# Per-machine harness overrides (never shared, may hold local paths/secrets).
.claude/settings.local.json

# --- Mongo mirror ---------------------------------------------------------
# No Mongo data directory and no dump ever lives inside the repo: the mirror
# holds the same unredacted transcripts .touch/ exists to protect.
mongo-data/
mongo-dump/
# *.bson is unanchored on purpose (dumps land wherever mongodump is run). If a
# .bson ever needs to be a committed test fixture, negate it explicitly rather
# than narrowing this rule: !tests/fixtures/**/*.bson
*.bson

